oomd/session — the whole Plasma session is spared, and the right app goes.

Every name kdos-oomd protects runs here, each LARGER than the victim and each
a different size: kwin_wayland and its wrapper, plasmashell, ksmserver, kded6,
plasma_session, kglobalacceld, the lock screen's greeter, Xwayland, the KDE
portal, the polkit agent, ksecretd, sddm with its helper and greeter, elogind,
turnstiled, the buses, ksvc, the KDOS daemons, accounts-daemon, wireplumber
and pipewire.

The names are what /proc/<pid>/stat carries, which is the executable's name
cut at 15 characters: kwin_wayland_wrapper is `kwin_wayland_wr`,
kscreenlocker_greet is `kscreenlocker_g`, xdg-desktop-portal-kde is
`xdg-desktop-por`, polkit-kde-authentication-agent-1 is `polkit-kde-auth`
and sddm-greeter-qt6 is `sddm-greeter-qt`. A list entry spelled in full
matches nothing, and the process it was meant to spare is the one chosen.

Outside the session there are two processes, kate (600 MB) and baloo_file
(200 MB). The answer is kate. Any other answer names the protection that
stopped holding, because it is the largest process left.
